## FAQ

**Q: Does Qmax Systems provide end-to-end PCB design services?**
A: Yes. Full PCB design cycle - schematic capture and stack-up planning to detailed layout, signal integrity analysis, and Gerber generation. IPC-trained designers manage every step from initial netlist to fabrication-ready output.

**Q: What PCB technologies and complexities does Qmax Systems handle?**
A: 2-layer boards to 32+ layer HDI, rigid-flex, and mixed-signal PCBs. High-density BGA fanouts, controlled-impedance routing, blind and buried vias, and length-tuned high-speed channels.

**Q: Which PCB design CAD tools does Qmax Systems support?**
A: Altium Designer, Cadence Allegro, Mentor Xpedition, OrCAD, KiCad, and PADS.

**Q: Does Qmax Systems handle high-speed and signal integrity design?**
A: Yes. DDR4/DDR5, PCIe Gen5, USB 4.0, Ethernet up to 112G SerDes, and RF up to mmWave. Pre-layout and post-layout SI/PI/EMI simulations in Cadence Sigrity and Ansys SIwave.

**Q: Does Qmax Systems perform DFM and pre-fabrication reviews?**
A: Yes. Internal DFM, DFA, and DFT reviews before fabrication release, coordinating directly with manufacturing partners.

**Q: How does Qmax Systems protect our PCB design data and IP?**
A: Strict NDAs, access-controlled encrypted servers with role-based permissions and complete audit trails. 100% IP ownership by customer.